---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Disclaimer" description="Scam-Proof Money gives general information only. It is not legal or financial advice.">
  <div class="page">
    <h1>Disclaimer</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated: 22 November 2026</p>

    <h2>General information only</h2>
    <p>
      Everything on this site is general information to help you recognize common scams. It is not legal,
      financial, tax or professional advice. We are not lawyers or financial advisers. For advice about your
      own situation, speak to your bank, a qualified professional or the official agency in your country.
    </p>

    <h2>We can't confirm a specific message</h2>
    <p>
      We can't tell you whether a particular text, call, email or website is real or fake. The checker and
      the guides describe common patterns. A message with no warning signs can still be a scam, and one with
      warning signs is not always a scam. When in doubt, contact the real company or person yourself, using
      a number you look up or already have.
    </p>

    <h2>Rules change</h2>
    <p>
      Scams, laws and bank policies change, and they differ by country, state and bank. We show the date each
      guide was last reviewed and list our sources. We try to keep the guides accurate, but we can't promise
      they are complete or current. Check the official source before you rely on a detail.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      We link to government agencies, banks and news outlets so you can check our facts. We don't control
      those sites and aren't responsible for their content.
    </p>

    <h2>In an emergency</h2>
    <p>
      If someone is in danger, call your local emergency number. If you think a family member is in trouble,
      hang up and call them directly on a number you already have.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
